 "text": "Hey, how's your day treating you? Stand your bike upright without a stand, sitting on a mat or carpet, so it doesn't get scratches. Stand the bike up against a wall with a mirror behind it, so you can see the seat post tube. Put a ruler where the seat post tube does, so you remember which end is up. That's the seat tube. You want your sit bone to just touch it there, not at the saddle clip bolt, and not so much upfront that your back hurts. Longer seats can be folded down, usually there's a little pin under the seat bowl. Shortening may need a different brand seat post.",
